    "title": "Who's in Elite 8? Updated March Madness bracket, NCAA Tournament schedule",
    "text": "Updated March 28, 2026, 8:37 p.m. ETThe Road to Indianapolis is set with the 2026 Elite Eight.The remaining teams in the Men's NCAA Tournament will go head-to-head in hopes of advancing one step closer to making that trip to Lucas Oil Stadium and Indianapolis for the Final Four.Three of the four No. 1 seeds have survived through the Sweet 16, including the Duke Blue Devils and Michigan Wolverines, who both won their games on Friday, March 27, despite early scares.No. 9 Iowa became the first team to clinch a berth in the Elite Eight, which came from behind to beat No. 4 seed Nebraska out of the South Region, 77-71. No. 1 Arizona, No. Purdue and No. 3 Tennessee all followed suit and advanced later that day.No. 2 Connecticut and No. 6 Tennessee joined the Blue Devils and Wolverines with wins on Friday. Half of the Elite Eight field will feature Big Ten teams, while the Big 12 (Arizona), SEC (Tennessee), Big East (UConn) and ACC (Duke) will each have one representative in the Elite Eight.Here's an updated look at which teams will advance to the Elite Eight, including updated brackets, matchups and schedules:Who's in men's Elite 8? Updated March Madness bracketNo. 1 Duke (East)No. 1 Michigan (Midwest)No. 1 Arizona (West)No. 2 UConn (East)No. 2 Purdue (West)No. 3 Illinois (South)No. 6 Tennessee (Midwest)No. 9 Iowa (South)Elite 8 schedule, game times, TV info, Elite 8 locationsAll times EasternGames held at Toyota Center in Houston (South Region), SAP Center in San Jose (West Region), Capital One Arena in Washington, D.C. (East Region), and United Center in Chicago (Midwest Region).Saturday, March 28South Region: No. 9 Iowa vs. No. 3 Illinois | 6:09 p.m. ET | TBS/truTV (Sling TV)West Region: No. 2 Purdue vs. No. 1 Arizona | (TBS/truTV) | 8:49 p.m. ET | TBS/truTV (Sling TV)Sunday, March 29Midwest Region: No. 1 Michigan vs. No. 6 Tennessee | (CBS) | 2:15 p.m. ET | (Fubo, free trial)East Region: No. 1 Duke vs No. 2 UConn | (CBS) | 5:05 p.m. ET | (Fubo, free trial)Elite 8 predictions: Who will advance to Final Four?USA TODAY Sports staff made their picks. Check them out here.March Madness 2026 bracket updateThis section will be updatedEast RegionFirst RoundNo. 1 Duke 71, No. 16 Siena 65No. 2 UConn 82, No. 15 Furman 71No. 3 Michigan State 92, No. 14 North Dakota State 67No. 4 Kansas 68, No. 13 California Baptist 60No. 5 St. John's 79, No. 12 Northern Iowa 53No. 6 Louisville 83, No. 11 South Florida 79No. 7 UCLA 75, No. 10 Central Florida 71No. 9 TCU 66, No. 8 Ohio State 64Second roundNo. 1 Duke 81, No. 9 TCU 58No. 5 St. John's 67, No. 4 Kansas 65No. 3 Michigan State 77, Louisville 69No. 2 UConn 73, No. 7 UCLA 57Sweet 16No. 1 Duke 80, No. 5 St. John's 75No. 2 UConn 67, No. 3 Michigan State 63Elite EightNo. 1 Duke vs No. 2 UConn | (CBS) | 5:05 p.m. ET on Sunday, March 29 | (Fubo, free trial)Midwest RegionFirst RoundNo. 1 Michigan 101, No. 16 Howard 80No. 2 Iowa State 108, No. 15 Tennessee State 74No. 3 Virginia 82, No. 14 Wright State 73No. 4 Alabama 90, No. 13 Hofstra 70No. 5 Texas Tech 91, No. 12 Howard 71No. 6 Tennessee 78, No. 11 Miami (Ohio) 56No. 7 Kentucky 89, No. 10 Santa Clara 84 (OT)No. 9 Saint Louis 102, No. 8 Georgia 77Second roundNo. 1 Michigan 95, No. 9 Saint Louis 72No. 4 Alabama 90, No. 5 Texas Tech 65No. 6 Tennessee 79, No. 3 Virginia 72No. 2 Iowa State 82, No. 7 Kentucky 63Sweet 16No. 1 Michigan 90, No. 4 Alabama 77No. 6 Tennessee 76, No. 2 Iowa State 62Elite EightNo. 1 Michigan vs No. 6 Tennessee | (CBS) | 2:15 p.m. ET on Sunday, March 29 | (Fubo, free trial)South RegionFirst RoundNo. 1 Florida 114, No. 16 Prairie View A&M 55No. 2 Houston 78, No. 15 Idaho 47No. 3 Illinois 105, No. 14 Penn 70No. 4 Nebraska 76, No. 13 Troy 47No. 5 Vanderbilt 78, No. 12 McNeese 68No. 11 VCU 82, No. 6 North Carolina 78No. 10 Texas A&M 63, No. 7 Saint Mary's 50No. 9 Iowa 67, No. 8 Clemson 61Second roundNo. 9 Iowa 73, No. 1 Florida 72No. 4 Nebraska 76, No. 5 Vanderbilt 74No. 3 Illinois 76, No. 11 VCU 55No. 2 Houston 88, No. 10 Texas A&M 57Sweet 16No. 9 Iowa 77, No. 4 Nebraska 71No. 3 Illinois 65, No. 2 Houston 55Elite EightNo. 3 Illinois 71, No. 9 Iowa 59West RegionFirst roundNo. 1 Arizona 82, No. 16 Long Island 58No. 2 Purdue 104, No. 15 Queens 71No. 3 Gonzaga 73, No. 14 Kennesaw State 64No. 4 Arkansas 97, No. 13 Hawai'i 78No. 12 High Point 83, No. 5 Wisconsin 82No. 11 Texas 79, No. 6 BYU 71No. 9 Utah State 86, No. 8 Villanova 76No. 7 Miami 80, No. 10 Missouri 66Second roundNo. 1 Arizona 78, No. 9 Utah State 66No. 4 Arkansas 94, No. 12 High Point 88No. 11 Texas 74, No. 3 Gonzaga 68No. 2 Purdue 79, No. 7 Miami 69Sweet 16No. 2 Purdue 79, No. 11 Texas 77No. 1 Arizona 109,No. 4 Arkansas 88Elite EightNo. 2 Purdue vs. No. 1 Arizona | 8:49 p.m. ET on Saturday, March 28 | TBS/truTV (Sling TV)The USA TODAY app gets you to the heart of the news — fast. Download for award-winning coverage, crosswords, audio storytelling, the eNewspaper and more.",
